PLACEHOLDER FOR RESUME TEMPLATE (.DOCX FILE)

This text file is a placeholder for "Nirajan_Resume.docx" which should be a Microsoft Word document (.docx format).

INSTRUCTIONS:
1. Create your resume in Microsoft Word and save it as "Nirajan_Resume.docx" in this directory
2. Your resume should be properly formatted with sections for:
   - Contact information
   - Professional summary
   - Skills (include all skills mentioned in your profile.json)
   - Work experience
   - Education
   - Projects (if applicable)

HOW AUTOJOBAGENT USES YOUR RESUME:
- The system will analyze job descriptions and identify missing keywords
- It will intelligently modify your resume to include relevant keywords
- Bullet points in your resume may be enhanced or modified
- A new "Skills" section might be added if needed keywords can't be naturally incorporated
- The customized resume will be converted to PDF before submission

IMPORTANT FORMATTING TIPS:
- Use bullet points (•) for experience and skills sections
- Keep formatting simple and ATS-friendly
- Avoid tables, text boxes, headers/footers, and complex formatting
- Use standard fonts like Calibri, Arial, or Times New Roman
- Include all your core skills as listed in your profile.json

Replace this placeholder file with your actual resume in .docx format before running AutoJobAgent.
